            <p class="section-label mb-3">Biography</p>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Academic Lead for Operations &amp; Finance | Brenkley Doctoral College</h2>
            <div class="space-y-4 text-muted">
              <p>Dr Elizabeth (Liz) Blower is Academic Lead for Operations &amp; Finance at Brenkley Doctoral College, where she holds senior responsibility for the effective operation of the College, financial oversight, researcher wellbeing, pastoral support, and the quality of the doctoral journey from initial induction through progression to successful completion.</p>
              <p>Dr Blower joined Brenkley Doctoral College following an academic and professional career spanning more than 30 years, encompassing retail management, educational research, management development and postgraduate student support at Northumbria University in Newcastle upon Tyne. This combination of industry and higher education experience gives her a strong understanding of the challenges faced by professionals undertaking advanced study alongside demanding careers and personal responsibilities.</p>
              <p>Her research background is principally within management practice, management development and human resource management. Her doctoral research examined the workplace experiences and career development of retail managers, exploring the personal and professional challenges associated with managing retail operations and the importance of appropriate professional development, workplace learning and formal education. Her work also considered how organisations can create more effective structures to support employee development, wellbeing and long-term career progression.</p>
              <p>This research and professional experience have directly influenced Dr Blower's contribution to the development of Brenkley Doctoral College's researcher wellbeing and pastoral support framework. Under her leadership, the College operates an annual pastoral review for every doctoral researcher, maintains an open-door approach to concerns relating to the researcher experience, and continues to develop peer-learning and researcher-community structures specifically designed to address the professional and personal challenges — including isolation — that can accompany doctoral study.</p>
              <p>Alongside her institutional leadership responsibilities, Dr Blower is an active and experienced doctoral supervisor. She currently provides supervision to eight doctoral researchers registered with the University of Greater Manchester, supporting them across the different stages of their doctoral journey. Her supervisory contribution includes research planning, methodological development, academic writing, researcher progression, professional development and preparation for successful doctoral completion.</p>
              <p>As a supervisor, Dr Blower has particular interests in research addressing professional education, organisational and employee wellbeing, management and leadership development, and qualitative approaches to understanding human experience. She is especially interested in supporting professionals working within healthcare, education and social care who are undertaking doctoral research into the wellbeing, development and professional experiences of the people they serve, support or lead.</p>
              <p>Through the combination of academic leadership, operational and financial oversight, researcher wellbeing, pastoral care and active doctoral supervision, Dr Blower plays a central role in ensuring that Brenkley Doctoral College provides a supportive, professionally relevant and high-quality doctoral environment. Her work reflects the College's commitment to seeing doctoral education not simply as the completion of a research qualification, but as a sustained process of researcher development, professional growth and personal transformation.</p>
            </div>
